---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";

const items = [
  ["Partial", "Paper-engine performance hardening", "Recursive deepcopy is removed; recent work indexes I3 crossings, H-tilde sources, and Extend projections. Remaining graph-sized snapshots, hierarchy work, and aggregate memory budgets still need migration and qualification."],
  ["In qualification", "Durable basic and multilevel modes", "Durable and Service select one of the two persisted paper modes. The former native matching engine is removed; exact recovery, failure-path and per-mode performance qualification remain."],
  ["Partial", "Repeatability, skew and adversarial qualification", "Earlier power-law and 60-second rates are historical results from the removed native matcher and do not qualify Basic or Multilevel. Repeatable paper-mode uniform/skewed, adversarial, hierarchy-boundary and recovery matrices remain."],
  ["Partial", "Service and deployment qualification", "Paper-backed local recovery, bounded-resource tests and operational guidance exist. Deployment supervision, broader skew/burst and explicit quota/alert policy remain. Hardware power-loss testing is deferred."],
  ["Not done", "Durable external vertex IDs", "Public graph labels are dense integers. Persistent UUID/string mapping and lifecycle semantics are absent."],
  ["Not done", "Dynamic vertex lifecycle", "The vertex universe is fixed at construction; durable add/remove semantics are absent."],
  ["Implemented; qualification active", "Atomic batch updates", "Durable Service has bounded atomic submit_batch with one SQLite commit boundary, exact retry and rollback tests. Installed-release and workload qualification remain."],
  ["Implemented, bounded", "Atomic multi-query read snapshots", "Service.read_snapshot returns immutable partner and edge-membership answers under one committed version with a 4096-query cap, stale-version rejection and serialized owner execution. This is not long-lived MVCC or historical topology retention."],
  ["Not done", "First-class bipartite API", "No typed partitions or same-side edge rejection contract exists."],
  ["Not done", "Event subscriptions", "Versioned change delivery, bounded subscriber queues and backpressure semantics are absent."],
  ["Partial", "Observability", "Service admission/group counters and benchmark histograms exist. Stable metrics/exporter, storage/recovery health and alert contracts remain."],
  ["Partial", "Deterministic replay and historical debugging", "Durable/Service history exports bounded retained operations with versions and chained digests; recovery replays and verifies state. Public import/replay verification and historical graph queries remain."],
  ["Not done", "Match explanations", "There is no version-linked explanation of partner changes or algorithm repair evidence."],
  ["Partial", "Cross-platform packaging", "CI/release matrices define 20 CPython wheels across five platform targets; hosted evidence is pending. Windows verifies native/paper APIs only because POSIX Durable/Service are unsupported there. Windows ARM64 and musllinux are excluded."],
  ["Not done", "Network transport", "Service is local and threaded; authenticated HTTP/gRPC transport and end-to-end network semantics are absent."],
  ["Future scope", "Weighted and constrained matching", "Weighted, maximum-cardinality and capacity-constrained matching remain separate future engine contracts."],
  ["Partial", "Machine-enforced release gates", "Research, quality and packaging gates exist. Paper-mode durable qualification and complete mode-specific release gates do not."],
] as const;
---
<DocLayout title="Product roadmap" eyebrow="17 requirements · evidence first" description="A requirement-by-requirement view of what exists, what is only partially qualified, and what still needs engineering." next={{ label: "Read research status", href: "/research/" }}>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Current boundary:</strong> Axiom exposes only paper-derived <code>basic</code> and <code>multilevel</code> matching through one Durable/Service path. The former native matching Engine has been removed; <code>Packed</code> remains compact graph storage. Atomic multi-update commits and operation-log recovery are implemented, but qualification is not complete: the latest 1M-vertex Multilevel smoke measured 3,136 updates/s at batch 256 (81 ms acknowledgment p99); a 4,096-operation atomic group measured 1,559/s (2.60 s p99). The 10k/s target remains unmet. Hardware power-loss is deferred; billion-vertex support is unproven.</p></div>
  <p>“Partial” means only the evidence stated exists; it does not imply the full requirement is met. Historical native-engine results do not qualify Basic or Multilevel.</p>
  <table class="doc-table">
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Status</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Evidence and remaining work</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{items.map(([status, title, detail], index) => <tr><td>{index + 1}</td><td>{status}</td><td><strong>{title}</strong></td><td>{detail}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Implementation-level decisions and benchmark artifacts are maintained alongside this roadmap in the repository. A claim is complete only when its stated gate passes on the relevant engine and packaging path.</p>
</DocLayout>
